# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0

# Positive fixture (applied-insurance-reference AIR-2.1, AIR-2.2, AIR-2.3): a small, real
# fragment of the cause scheme that passes every shape in structural.ttl and constraints.ttl.
# No owl:Ontology header: not a released document.
#
# Six cause concepts, all now declared for real in vocab/peril-vocab.ttl (AIR-2.3): two family
# tops (N, T), the N.MET / N.MET.TC path to them, N.MET.TC.SRG as a partitive part of N.MET.TC,
# and N.MET.TC.HUR as a generic kind of N.MET.TC, threshold-defined with a prl:definingThreshold.
# This fixture no longer re-declares their identity: AIR-2.3 made that redundant, and a
# re-declaration that drifted from the real text would itself be a second, distinct value,
# breaking LabelAndDefinitionShape's "exactly one" rule. Every threshold-defined cause concept's
# real prl:definingThreshold lives in vocab/peril-intensity.ttl (AIR-2.6), which every consumer
# of this fixture now loads alongside it (tools/test_peril_vocabulary.py,
# tools/test_peril_intensity.py), so this fixture adds no placeholder of its own.

@prefix prl:     <https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/insurance/peril#> .
@prefix prl-voc: <https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/insurance/peril/vocab#> .
@prefix qnt:     <https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/lattice/quantification#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix ex:      <https://example.org/lattice/insurance/peril/examples#> .


